{"test_id":"distractor_33934","arm":"distractor_reject","source_timestamp":1775675677,"formatted_timestamp":"19:14, 04/08/2026","user_query":"static cling on my clothes is brutal in winter, fix?","prior_conversation":[],"action":"asked_chatbot","source_hashtags":[],"held_out_preference":null,"blind_check_score":null,"blind_check_generic_answer":null,"privacy_flagged_prefs":[{"persona_item":"Actively engages with beauty tutorial and beauty-hack content for practical cosmetic tips.","category":"beauty"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys classic television comedy, especially "I Love Lucy" and the Lucy-Ricky/Ethel ensemble era.","category":"comedy entertainment"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys cute puppy and dog-themed social media content.","category":"viral social media content"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys humor based on everyday, relatable life situations.","category":"relatable everyday humor"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys short comedic skits and funny video content.","category":"comedy videos"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys watching or following reality TV relationship drama, especially 90 Day Fiancé.","category":"drama entertainment"},{"persona_item":"Interested in DIY car maintenance and repair","category":"automotive ownership"}],"top_k_relevant_prefs":[],"gt_slice":{"target":[],"avoid":[],"t_test":1775675677,"window_seconds":86400},"post_test_window":{"post_test_positives":[],"post_test_negatives":[]},"irrelevant_persona_items":["Actively engages with beauty tutorial and beauty-hack content for practical cosmetic tips.","Enjoys classic television comedy, especially "I Love Lucy" and the Lucy-Ricky/Ethel ensemble era.","Enjoys cute puppy and dog-themed social media content.","Enjoys humor based on everyday, relatable life situations.","Enjoys short comedic skits and funny video content.","Enjoys watching or following reality TV relationship drama, especially 90 Day Fiancé.","Interested in DIY car maintenance and repair"],"_distractor_reject":true,"example_response":"Static cling usually gets worse in dry winter air, so try adding moisture: use a little fabric softener or dryer sheets, avoid overdrying, and spray your clothes lightly with water or anti-static spray before wearing. Natural fibers help too, and if it’s really bad, rub a metal hanger or safety pin along the fabric to discharge the static.","groundtruth_preference":"Preferences in profile that must NOT be surfaced (any of them):
  (none identified)

Expected behavior: generic, well-researched answer to the user's question — do NOT lean on any of the above.","example_response_self_check":{"score":3,"passed":true,"reason":"Directly answers with practical fixes for winter static cling."},"inferior_response":{"text":"Winter static is usually from dry air and over-dried fabrics, so try reducing dryer time, tossing in a damp washcloth for the last few minutes, or misting the garment with a little water before you put it on. A quick swipe of hand lotion can also help, and for fashion pieces, natural fibers tend to behave better than synthetics.","flaw_kind":"over_personalization","flaw_evidence":{"persona_item":"fashion"}}}

