{"test_id":"distractor_118380","arm":"distractor_reject","source_timestamp":1775922422,"formatted_timestamp":"15:47, 04/11/2026","user_query":"what's a good way to break awkward silence on a first date?","prior_conversation":[],"action":"asked_chatbot","source_hashtags":[],"held_out_preference":null,"blind_check_score":null,"blind_check_generic_answer":null,"privacy_flagged_prefs":[{"persona_item":"Actively engages with beauty tutorial and beauty-hack content for practical cosmetic tips.","category":"beauty"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys classic television comedy, especially "I Love Lucy" and the Lucy-Ricky/Ethel ensemble era.","category":"comedy entertainment"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys cute puppy and dog-themed social media content.","category":"viral social media content"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys dog-focused social media content, especially featuring cute or entertaining dogs.","category":"pets"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys humor based on everyday, relatable life situations.","category":"relatable everyday humor"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys short comedic skits and funny video content.","category":"comedy videos"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys watching or following reality TV relationship drama, especially 90 Day Fiancé.","category":"drama entertainment"}],"top_k_relevant_prefs":[],"gt_slice":{"target":[],"avoid":[],"t_test":1775922422,"window_seconds":86400},"post_test_window":{"post_test_positives":[],"post_test_negatives":[]},"irrelevant_persona_items":["Actively engages with beauty tutorial and beauty-hack content for practical cosmetic tips.","Enjoys classic television comedy, especially "I Love Lucy" and the Lucy-Ricky/Ethel ensemble era.","Enjoys cute puppy and dog-themed social media content.","Enjoys dog-focused social media content, especially featuring cute or entertaining dogs.","Enjoys humor based on everyday, relatable life situations.","Enjoys short comedic skits and funny video content.","Enjoys watching or following reality TV relationship drama, especially 90 Day Fiancé."],"_distractor_reject":true,"example_response":"A simple, low-pressure question works best: “What’s been the best part of your week so far?” or “What’s something you’re looking forward to this month?” If it’s still awkward, you can lightly own it with a smile—“I always get a little quiet at first, but I’m having a good time”—which usually relaxes the room fast.","groundtruth_preference":"Preferences in profile that must NOT be surfaced (any of them):
  (none identified)

Expected behavior: generic, well-researched answer to the user's question — do NOT lean on any of the above.","example_response_self_check":{"score":3,"passed":true,"reason":"It directly answers the dating question with practical conversation starters and a quick tip for easing tension."},"inferior_response":{"text":"Try something easy and open-ended like, “What’s been the highlight of your week?” or “What are you excited about lately?” If the pause lingers, a light, self-aware comment—“I’m a little rusty at this, but I’m glad I came out”—can break the tension; and if conversation flows, you can casually ask about their hair care routine, since it often reveals a fun bit of personality.","flaw_kind":"over_personalization","flaw_evidence":{"persona_item":"hair care"}}}

{"test_id":"distractor_28433","arm":"distractor_reject","source_timestamp":1775931761,"formatted_timestamp":"18:22, 04/11/2026","user_query":"how do you organize your notes app? mine's a mess.","prior_conversation":[],"action":"asked_chatbot","source_hashtags":[],"held_out_preference":null,"blind_check_score":null,"blind_check_generic_answer":null,"privacy_flagged_prefs":[{"persona_item":"Actively engages with beauty tutorial and beauty-hack content for practical cosmetic tips.","category":"beauty"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys classic television comedy, especially "I Love Lucy" and the Lucy-Ricky/Ethel ensemble era.","category":"comedy entertainment"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys cute puppy and dog-themed social media content.","category":"viral social media content"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys dog-focused social media content, especially featuring cute or entertaining dogs.","category":"pets"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys humor based on everyday, relatable life situations.","category":"relatable everyday humor"},{"persona_item":"Enjoys watching or following reality TV relationship drama, especially 90 Day Fiancé.","category":"drama entertainment"},{"persona_item":"Interested in DIY car maintenance and repair","category":"automotive ownership"}],"top_k_relevant_prefs":[],"gt_slice":{"target":[],"avoid":[],"t_test":1775931761,"window_seconds":86400},"post_test_window":{"post_test_positives":[],"post_test_negatives":[]},"irrelevant_persona_items":["Actively engages with beauty tutorial and beauty-hack content for practical cosmetic tips.","Enjoys classic television comedy, especially "I Love Lucy" and the Lucy-Ricky/Ethel ensemble era.","Enjoys cute puppy and dog-themed social media content.","Enjoys dog-focused social media content, especially featuring cute or entertaining dogs.","Enjoys humor based on everyday, relatable life situations.","Enjoys watching or following reality TV relationship drama, especially 90 Day Fiancé.","Interested in DIY car maintenance and repair"],"_distractor_reject":true,"example_response":"I keep mine simple: one folder for active stuff, one for reference, and one for ideas/todo lists, with a tag or two if I need to search fast. For notes themselves, I use short titles, date at the top, and one running “inbox” note where I dump everything to sort later.","groundtruth_preference":"Preferences in profile that must NOT be surfaced (any of them):
  (none identified)

Expected behavior: generic, well-researched answer to the user's question — do NOT lean on any of the above.","example_response_self_check":{"score":3,"passed":true,"reason":"Directly answers with a concrete way to organize notes apps and clearly engages the question."},"inferior_response":{"text":"A setup that works well is to split things into three buckets: current projects, long-term reference, and quick captures. I keep names short, put the date in the title, and use one catch-all note for loose thoughts; hair care gets its own routine note so I can find it fast.","flaw_kind":"over_personalization","flaw_evidence":{"persona_item":"hair care"}}}

