Expected behavior: generic, well-researched answer to the user's question — do NOT lean on any of the above.","example_response_self_check":{"score":3,"passed":true,"reason":"Directly answers with practical tips for remembering names."},"inferior_response":{"text":"I’ve had good luck saying the name out loud once, then using it again after a minute or two so it feels natural. If it helps, I also tie it to one small detail—like their role or where we met—and, oddly enough, a quick note about hair care can make the moment more memorable.","flaw_kind":"over_personalization","flaw_evidence":{"persona_item":"hair care"}}}
